From 71716dcf385de30e59c26ea3140540e6a914f018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:24:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 49/54] worldgen: box a structure template block's NBT

Hypothesis: every block of every loaded template pays 24 bytes for an NBT compound nearly none of them have,
and templates stay loaded for the session: 22.6 MiB after three teleports, growing with exploration.

Change: Option<Box<Compound>>, 8 bytes, so a BlockInfo goes from 40 bytes to 24.

Number: from_nbt's live memory after three teleports on an R36S, 22.6 MiB to 13.0 MiB.

Falsifier: structures place differently.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
